    },
    "extraction_notes": [
      "NCE3407 is p-channel; all extracted electrical magnitudes are positive while conditions preserve the datasheet's negative p-channel signs.",
      "The datasheet publishes VGS(th) = -1 V minimum, -1.5 V typical, -3 V maximum at VDS = VGS and ID = -250 uA; these are recorded as magnitudes per the context-pack instruction.",
      "The datasheet publishes RDS(ON) at both VGS = -10 V, ID = -4.1 A and VGS = -4.5 V, ID = -4 A, with typical and maximum values; all four entries are preserved.",
      "The p. 3 to p. 4 characteristic plots are direct readings from the supplied figures. Curve axes and p-channel polarity are preserved in the curve metadata.",
      "The electrical table lists BVDSS typical -33 V in addition to the minimum -30 V; the strict schema has one breakdown-voltage field, so the guaranteed minimum magnitude is recorded.",
      "The electrical table lists IDSS maximum -1 uA at VDS = -24 V, VGS = 0 V, and gate charge Qg typical 12.5 nC, Qgs typical 2.8 nC, Qgd typical 2.7 nC; the strict schema has no dedicated fields for these values."
    ],
    "family": "mosfet",
